ntfs-3g (ntfs-macos) patch 0010: ntfs_valid_descr() checks the length before it reads the header

Rationale (T-M3-25, ADR-026, finding F3, GHSA-g3h3-7rhv-rrmq, tests/fuzz/TRIAGE.md): in NTFS-3G 2026.9.28,
libntfs-3g/acls.c ntfs_valid_descr(securattr, attrsz) reads phead->dacl, phead->sacl, phead->owner and
phead->group (lines 682 to 685) before it compares attrsz with sizeof(SECURITY_DESCRIPTOR_RELATIVE)
(line 695). The comment before the check says the size test comes before the pointers are used; that is
true for the derived pointers but not for the four header fields. getsecurityattr() (security.c:1892 to
1894) passes it the result of ntfs_attr_readall() for $SECURITY_DESCRIPTOR, which can be shorter than the
header or empty (a one-byte attribute makes ASan report a heap-buffer-overflow read of 4 bytes; valgrind on
the unmodified library shows "Invalid read of size 4" at acls.c:682). The function is reached from every
permission check (-o permissions) and from getxattr system.ntfs_acl.
Change (libntfs-3g/acls.c, one hunk): return FALSE at the top of ntfs_valid_descr() when
attrsz < sizeof(SECURITY_DESCRIPTOR_RELATIVE), before any header field is read. The existing "attrsz >=
sizeof(SECURITY_DESCRIPTOR_RELATIVE)" term in the long condition stays (now always true there).
Scope: library-wide and cross-platform (no __APPLE__ guard). It only adds a rejection of a malformed
on-disk descriptor; a descriptor of at least the header size takes the same path as before. The callers
already treat FALSE as "invalid descriptor" and log the error.
Upstream status: reported privately 2026-11-16 as GHSA-g3h3-7rhv-rrmq; carried until a fixed NTFS-3G release
is pinned, then removed (ADR-026).
Test: ctest fuzz.findings.F3 replays tests/fuzz/image/findings/F3-valid-descr-heap-overflow.bin through
fuzz_replay_mountwalk (security reads on), registered only for an ASan build. Verified in Environment A: on
the unpatched library it fails (heap-buffer-overflow at acls.c:682) with clang -O0 and -O1, gcc -O0, and
gcc -O1 with -fsanitize=address,undefined; it does NOT fail unpatched with gcc -O1 and -fsanitize=address
alone (the compiler removes the header loads, which are used only after the length test), so there it
only shows that the patched library does not crash. It passes with the patch in every one of those builds.
The standalone image replayed under valgrind (repro_secdesc): "Invalid read of size 4" at acls.c:682
unpatched, none patched.

--- a/libntfs-3g/acls.c
+++ b/libntfs-3g/acls.c
@@ -672,6 +672,13 @@
 
 	ok = TRUE;
 
+		/*
+		 * a descriptor shorter than its header cannot be read
+		 * (ntfs-macos 0010)
+		 */
+	if (attrsz < sizeof(SECURITY_DESCRIPTOR_RELATIVE))
+		return (FALSE);
+
 	/*
 	 * first check overall size if within allocation range
 	 * and a DACL is present
